Third-party models and effect textures in forge-ordnance-arsenal.bundle. Each was downloaded free under the
licence shown on its page, then re-oriented, scaled and re-exported for the game (flat colours of the low-poly models merged
into one small palette texture; textured models keep their own textures, resized, with the ambient occlusion multiplied into the
base colour; effect textures converted to white-on-alpha and packed into atlases). The originals are not included.

Gun models, from Sketchfab per the project owner (the downloads hold no licence text and no record of author or page):

- "heavy-mg": Minimi light machine gun (file "minimi.fbx").
  Modified: the carry handle, rear sight and front sight post are removed, the ammo box is a separate part, and the reflex sight below is fitted on the top cover.
- "anti-materiel-rifle": B&T SPR 300 (file "B&T SPR 300.fbx").
  Modified: the telescopic sight is removed, the mesh is reduced from about 51,000 to about 42,000 triangles, the magazine is a separate part and the reflex sight below is fitted on the top rail.
- "tracking-rifle": Honey Badger (file "game ready honeybadger").
  Modified: the optic, its lens and the laser beam are removed, the magazine is a separate part, and the reflex sight below is fitted on the top rail.

Gun model, Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):

- "grenade-launcher": "RG-6 Grenade Launcher" by Sassiska (https://sketchfab.com/Sassiska),
  https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/rg-6-grenade-launcher-d911c28d568c4dec838d67760f323d98, CC BY 4.0.
  Modified: the folding leaf sight and the front sight post are removed and the reflex sight below is fitted on the top tube.

Models generated for this project by its owner with a paid Tripo subscription (commercial use included) and repaired for the game: "shell", "shell-precision", "shell-hunter", "shell-incendiary", "bomblet", "rocket",
"grenade-40", "gas-canister", "stasis-emitter", "mine", "glue-mine", "recoilless", "turret-burst", "turret-sniper", "turret-shotgun", "dispenser", "radar", "floodlight".

Sight on the four guns, Creative Commons Zero (public domain dedication; credit given anyway):

- "Red Dot Sight" by Jean PFP, https://opengameart.org/content/red-dot-sight, CC0 1.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). Modified: scaled to 10 cm, recoloured dark, a red dot added at the window centre.

Effect textures, Creative Commons Zero (public domain dedication; credit given anyway):

- vfx-flare, vfx-spark: from "Particle Pack" by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/particle-pack), CC0.
- vfx-smoke: "Smoke Aura" by Beast, posted by tehwave (https://opengameart.org/content/smoke-aura), CC0.
- vfx-fireball: frames of the Unity Labs VFX image sequence (FireBall02), CC0 1.0 (https://unity.com/blog/engine-platform/free-vfx-image-sequences-flipbooks), downsized and packed by tools/make_unitylabs_atlases.py.
- vfx-ring, vfx-scorch, vfx-streak, vfx-glow: drawn for this package by tools/make_fx_textures.py (own work, CC0).

Downloaded on 2026-10-24 (grenade-launcher), 2026-10-28 (the sight) and 2026-11-04 (heavy-mg, anti-materiel-rifle, tracking-rifle).
